<<
/Title (In 1980 there were roughly 26 million Americans over 65. By 2030, that number will exceed 73 million, and by 2050, 86 million. The share of the U.S. population that is 65+ will cross 21% before this decade ends. Every major surgical specialty will see its case mix shift towards older and more complex adults.)
