1647 0 obj
<<
/Title (Hip and femur fracture treatment is overwhelmingly an older-adult procedure \(~78%\); CABG, joint replacement, spinal fusion, and major bowel surgery all draw much of their volume from the 65+ population. This is the operational reality TEAM was written for: the procedures with the highest age skew older with the highest variation in post-acute spending, and the highest readmission rates. These five surgical focus areas contain the same procedures CMS is now requiring hospitals to manage as full episodes, beyond the hospital inpatient stay, with a focus on reduced spending while optimizing surgical outcomes and the care experience.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1588 0 R
/Prev 1658 0 R
/First 1659 0 R
/Last 1660 0 R
/Count -2
/Next 1628 0 R
